WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:05.820
In 1877, the philosopher W K
Clifford made a bold claim.

2
00:00:05.870 --> 00:00:10.930
It is wrong, he said, to believe
anything on insufficient evidence.

3
00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:15.530
Yet we believe in friends, teachers and
doctors long before we could prove them

4
00:00:15.580 --> 00:00:16.850
reliable.

5
00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:19.990
Some philosophers say
Clifford asks too much.

6
00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:21.880
Others say he is right.

7
00:00:21.930 --> 00:00:25.300
So can a belief be
reasonable, and make sense,

8
00:00:25.350 --> 00:00:28.390
yet rest on trust rather than proof?

9
00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:31.350
In this mission, you'll test
beliefs the way philosophers do:

10
00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:35.300
are they reasonable,
meaningful and coherent?

11
00:00:35.350 --> 00:00:40.530
Then you'll split believing that something
is true from believing in someone.

12
00:00:40.580 --> 00:00:45.480
Your mission: find out whether a belief
can be reasonable yet rest on trust.
